+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    ArrayList - data structure for storing sequences
                * fast random access O(1)
                * append: O(1) amortized
                * insertion/removal in the middle O(n)

    Internals:
        * Internally backed by an array

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    LinkedList - data structure for storing sequences
                 * random access O(n)
                 * insertion/removal at known node/ends O(1)
                 * generally less efficient that ArrayList

    Internals:
        * Internally backed by liked nodes

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    HashMap - data structure for storing key-value pairs that offers O(1) complexity for
              get/put operations on average (can degrade with collisions)


    Internals:
        * Internally represented as an array of buckets
            * Buckets initially use linked lists
            * Buckets may be converted to red-black trees when sufficiently large
        * The array is resized when size > capacity × loadFactor

        Size vs Capacity:
            * Size     - number of key-value pairs currently stored
            * Capacity - number of buckets in the internal array

        Defaults:
            * loadFactor: 0.75
            * initial capacity: 16


    How it works:
        Put:
            1. Compute a hash from the key's hashCode()
            2. Use the hash to determine the bucket
            3. Check entries already in that bucket
                a. If a key for which equals() is true is found -> replace its value
                b. If no equal key exists                       -> add a new entry

    Null key handling:
        1 null key allowed

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    HashSet - data structure for storing unique elements that offers O(1) complexity for a
              add/contains operations

    Internals:
        * Internally it is backed by a HashMap
            * key   -> set element
            * value -> dummy constant object

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    LinkedHashMap - data structure wth all functionalities of a HashMap while also preserving
                    insertion order

    Internals:
        * Internally backed by a hashtable + a doubly linked list for preserving order of inserts

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    LinkedHashSet - data structure with all functionalities of a HashSet while also preserving
                    insertion order

    Internals:
        * Internally backed by a LinkedHashMap
            * key   -> set element
            * value -> dummy constant object

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    TreeMap - data structure for storing sorted key-value pairs that offers O(log n) complexity
              for get/put operations

    Internals:
        * Internally represented as a red-black tree
        * Keys are ordered by their natural ordering or a provided comparator

        Natural ordering - key must implement Comparable

    Null key handling:
        * null not allowed with natural ordering
        * null allowed if handled in provided comparator

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    TreeSet - data structure for storing unique elements that offers O(log n) complexity
              for add/contains operations

        Internals:
            * Internally backed by a TreeMap
                * key   -> set element
                * value -> dummy constant object

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    Collections.synchronizedMap - thread-safe wrapper around a map that synchronizes individual
                                  operations

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    ConcurrentHashMap - thread-safe alternative to HashMap that achieves thread-safety by
                        * utilizing CAS (compare-and-swap) for certain operations
                        * localized locking (e.g. locking a specific bucket when necessary)

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    CopyOnWriteArrayList - thread-safe alternative to ArrayList that achieves thread-safety by
                           creating a copy of the underlying array on every write
                           * reads can happen without locking and are very efficient
                           * existing iterators see the snapshot of the array that existed when
                             the iterator was created

    Use cases:
        * more reads than writes

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    BlockingQueue - thread-safe queue commonly used for producer-consumer scenarios
                    * Blocks when queue is full  (producer waits)
                    * Blocks when queue is empty (consumer waits)


    Implementations:
        * ArrayBlockingQueue - implementation of BlockingQueue backed by a fixed size array
                               * capacity is fixed when queue is created
                               * uses one lock for put and take operations

        * LinkedBlockingQueue - implementation of BlockingQueue backed by a linked list
                                * capacity can be optionally provided
                                * uses separate locks for put and take operations, allowing
                                  producer and consumer to work concurrently

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

    ConcurrentLinkedQueue - thread-safe, non-blocking implementation of queue
                            * Unbounded - doesn't block when adding elements
                            * Doesn't block when queue is empty (returns null)

